pe":"1","question":" <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Which of the following is a famous historical gateway located in Gaur, West Bengal?</span></p>","option_1":"Dakhil Darwaza","option_2":"Buland Darwaza","option_3":"Rumi Darwaza","option_4":"Alai Darwaza","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":" <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - Dakhil Darwaza.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span> </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Dakhil Darwaza is a large brick-built ceremonial gateway situated at Gaur (an ancient capital city) in the Malda district of West Bengal, built during the Sultanate period. Buland Darwaza is at Fatehpur Sikri, Rumi Darwaza is in Lucknow, and Alai Darwaza is part of the Qutub complex in Delhi.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29643","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"770","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":" <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">How many gold medals has India won in athletics till Paris Olympics 2024?</span></p>","option_1":"1","option_2":"2","option_3":"3","option_4":"4","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","image_link_1":"","image_link_2":"","image_link_3":"","answer":"1","solution_heading":"Full Solution","solution_text":" <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>Correct Answer: Option A - 1.</span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:10pt\"><span> </span></p><p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span>India has won only one Olympic gold medal in athletics to date — by Neeraj Chopra in the Men's Javelin Throw at the Tokyo 2020 Olympics (held in 2021). At the Paris 2024 Olympics, Neeraj Chopra won a silver medal, so India's athletics gold-medal tally remained at 1 through the Paris Games.</span></p>","solution_image_1":"","solution_image_2":"","solution_video":"","difficulty_level":"0","topic":"","exam":"","section_id":"4","subject":"","concept":"","report_count":"0","set_no":"0","positive_marks":"3.00","negative_marks":"1.00","sortingparam":"0.00","question_heading":"","directive":"","deleted":"0","image_check":"0","subject_title":"","concept_title":"","topic_title":""},{"id":"29644","test_series_id":"2","test_id":"770","question_type":"1","question_ui_type":"1","question":" <p style=\"margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-weight:bold\">Rawatbhata Atomic Power Plant is located near which city?</span></p>","option_1":"Jaipur","option_2":"Udaipur","option_3":"Ajmer","option_4":"Kota","option_5":"","option_6":"","option_7":"","option_8":"","option_9":"","option_10":"","option_image_1":"","option_image_2":"","option_image_3":"","option_image_4":"","option_image_5":"","option_image_6":"","option_image_7":"","option_image_8":"","option_image_9":"","option_image_10":"","im